# `mismatch`: a block's signature line types the `let` under it, as a top-level one types
# its definition: `xs` is a `[Bool]`, so a text element is refused. Written by Claude on the
# claude-bugs branch; subject to change.
Size: fn Nat -> Nat
fn Size n:
    xs: [Bool]
    let xs = [["a"]]
    Len xs
